SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei Issues Decree To Set Up A Social Safety Net","publisher":"Iran International","publication_date":"2022-04-10","url":"https://www.iranintl.com/en/202204109399","claim":"Khamenei issued policies aimed at improving social welfare, reducing poverty, and supporting vulnerable groups, and ordered the executive branch to produce an implementation plan within six months.","locator":"lines 47-55","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous report on a specific decree, but from a media outlet rather than the original Persian text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022 and within the target ruler-period","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: the proclamation is presented as Khamenei's own directive to the heads of power; it shows personal agenda-setting, not proof of delivery.","contrary_evidence":["The article notes no dedicated funding and says the directive is a brief, general guideline."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Leader Communicates General Policies of Iran's 7th Development Plan","publisher":"Tasnim News Agency","publication_date":"2022-09-12","url":"https://www.tasnimnews.ir/en/news/2022/09/12/2773351/leader-communicates-general-policies-of-iran-s-7th-development-plan","claim":"Khamenei outlined the 7th development plan as a five-year program centered on economic progress with justice and an 8 percent growth target, with food-security and national information-network measures among the stated priorities.","locator":"lines 56-70","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The report quotes and summarizes a specific proclamation and gives detailed policy content, though it is still a news report rather than the original decree text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022 and within the target ruler-period","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: the item reports a proclamation by Khamenei sent to top state leaders, reflecting his agenda-setting power.","contrary_evidence":["The article describes planned goals; it does not prove implementation or attainment in 2022.","Later macro outcomes remained stressed by inflation and hardship in other sources."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNICEF and Ministry of Labour discussed enhancing social protection systems for children","publisher":"UNICEF Iran","publication_date":"2022-04-28","url":"https://www.unicef.org/iran/en/press-releases/unicef-and-ministry-labour-discussed-enhancing-social-protection-systems-children","claim":"Iran's child social protection system was presented as targeting vulnerable households, especially in less advantaged provinces, using a welfare database of deprived households and a cash-plus model in selected provinces.","locator":"lines 64-73","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UNICEF is an official UN agency and the page describes a specific national policy discussion and implementation architecture.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022 and within the target ruler-period","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: this shows the state apparatus and welfare ministry implementing a child social-protection architecture under the Supreme Leader's governing framework, but it is not a personal decree from Khamenei.","contrary_evidence":["This describes a webinar and system presentation, not an independent outcome evaluation.","It does not quantify coverage gains or prove Khamenei's direct day-to-day management."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Education","publisher":"UNHCR Iran","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.unhcr.org/ir/education","claim":"UNHCR says all children in Iran have access to primary and secondary education regardless of documentation status, and that it co-funded 81 schools in refugee-populated areas between 2016 and 2022.","locator":"lines 110-124","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UNHCR is the relevant UN agency and the page contains specific operational claims about access and school construction, though it is a current web page rather than a dated 2022 report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"policy and implementation context spans 2016-2022 and remains relevant to the 2022 period","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: this is evidence of government-compatible refugee access policy and UNHCR implementation in Iran, but not direct proof that Khamenei personally ran the program day to day.","contrary_evidence":["The page is not time-stamped for 2022 and does not provide household survey outcomes.","It does not isolate Khamenei from broader state or UNHCR implementation."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Health workers in Iran reach out to families of children with measles to vaccinate all family member","publisher":"UNICEF Iran","publication_date":"2022-07-21","url":"https://www.unicef.org/iran/en/stories/health-workers-iran-reach-out-families-children-measles-vaccinate-all-family-member","claim":"In July 2022, Iran ran a targeted measles vaccination campaign for children and vulnerable communities; refugee families without immigration documents were vaccinated, and the article says confirmed cases fell dramatically.","locator":"lines 70-81","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UNICEF provides a dated field story with concrete operational details, named beneficiaries, and an explicit 2022 campaign result, though it is still a program story rather than an audit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022 and within the target ruler-period","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful: the campaign shows government health services functioning for refugees and vulnerable households under the regime, but it does not isolate Khamenei's personal operational role.","contrary_evidence":["The evidence is narrative and does not independently audit causality for the decline in cases.","It does not show whether the campaign was ordered by Khamenei rather than the health ministry."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I kept 5 new source-claim units and treated the rest as supporting context or duplicates of already indexed material.
- I rejected a blocked route to the compiled Nezamat policy mirror because open access returned 403, so I relied on accessible contemporaneous reporting instead.
- I rejected several broad or overlapping hits that did not add new ruler-specific evidence, including commentary-only pieces, post-2022 explainers, and pages that repeated the same Khamenei slogan or macroeconomic context already covered by the existing index.
- The only concrete 2022 personnel item I found for the economy remained the cabinet-level central bank appointment already in the existing index (`E0049`), which is useful as a limit on direct attribution but does not fill the personal-appointment gap.

**Remaining Gaps**
- Direct Khamenei-linked economic implementation or appointments: partly resolved. The 2022 social-safety-net decree and the 7th-plan proclamation now show direct policy direction, but I still did not find a direct 2022 economic appointment by Khamenei. That appointment subgap is not recoverable from open sources I checked.
- Direct Khamenei-linked social-policy decisions or corrective interventions in 2022: partly resolved. The social-safety-net decree and the 7th-plan directive show direct intervention, but evidence of concrete corrective follow-through after failure remains thin.
- Independent household/service-quality evidence on who benefited: partly resolved. The UN agency material now shows refugees, less-advantaged provinces, undocumented families, and vulnerable children as explicit beneficiaries, but household survey or audited outcome evidence is still missing.
- More search would help most for the third gap, somewhat for the second, and only marginally for the appointment subgap.
